---
description: Flutter project file organization standards for Monica Companion app defining feature-first architecture, directory structure conventions, and file placement rules. Ensures consistent project organization with clear separation between core utilities, features, services, and test mirroring for maintainable scalable codebase.
globs: ["lib/**", "test/**", "integration_test/**"]
alwaysApply: true
---

## Root Directory Structure

- Keep lib/ as main source
- Mirror test/ structure exactly
- Place core utilities in core/
- Group features under features/
- Isolate services in services/

```
lib/
├── core/           # Shared utilities and configurations
├── features/       # Feature-specific modules
├── services/       # Application services
├── config/         # App-wide configuration
├── db/            # Database related code
└── main.dart      # Application entry point
```

## Core Directory Organization

- Place configs in core/config/
- Put utilities in core/utils/
- Store errors in core/errors/
- Keep constants in core/constants/
- Organize by functional purpose

```
core/
├── config/
│   ├── app_config.dart      # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
│   └── environment.dart     # @lib/core/config/environment.dart
├── utils/
│   ├── logger.dart          # @lib/core/utils/logger.dart
│   └── validators.dart      # @lib/core/utils/validators.dart
├── errors/
│   ├── exceptions.dart      # @lib/core/errors/exceptions.dart
│   └── failures.dart        # @lib/core/errors/failures.dart
└── constants/
    └── app_constants.dart   # @lib/core/constants/app_constants.dart
```

## Feature Directory Structure

- Use feature-first architecture pattern
- Create shared/ for common components
- Each feature contains complete module
- Group by business domain
- Include models, widgets, utils

```
features/
├── shared/                  # Shared across features
│   ├── models/
│   │   └── feature_state.dart    # @lib/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart
│   ├── widgets/
│   │   ├── error_widget.dart     # @lib/features/shared/widgets/error_widget.dart
│   │   ├── loading_widget.dart   # @lib/features/shared/widgets/loading_widget.dart
│   │   └── empty_state_widget.dart
│   └── utils/
│       └── feature_utils.dart    # @lib/features/shared/utils/feature_utils.dart
└── [feature_name]/         # Individual feature modules
    ├── models/
    ├── widgets/
    ├── screens/
    └── utils/
```

## Services and Configuration

- Place service locator in services/
- Keep database code in db/
- Store feature flags in config/
- Separate interface definitions clearly
- Group related functionality together

```
services/
└── service_locator.dart     # @lib/services/service_locator.dart

db/
├── models/
│   └── base_model.dart      # @lib/db/models/base_model.dart
├── repositories/
│   └── base_repository.dart # @lib/db/repositories/base_repository.dart
├── interfaces/
│   ├── repository_interface.dart  # @lib/db/interfaces/repository_interface.dart
│   └── database_interface.dart    # @lib/db/interfaces/database_interface.dart
└── database_config.dart     # @lib/db/database_config.dart
```

## Test Directory Mirroring

- Mirror lib/ structure exactly
- Use same directory names
- Include helper utilities in helpers/
- Group mocks in mocks/
- Follow naming convention consistently

```
test/
├── mocks/
│   └── mock_services.dart   # @test/mocks/mock_services.dart
├── helpers/
│   └── test_helpers.dart    # @test/helpers/test_helpers.dart
├── core/
│   └── utils/
│       ├── validators_test.dart  # @test/core/utils/validators_test.dart
│       └── logger_test.dart      # @test/core/utils/logger_test.dart
├── config/
│   └── environment_test.dart     # @test/config/environment_test.dart
├── app_test.dart            # @test/app_test.dart
└── widget_test.dart         # @test/widget_test.dart
```

## File Placement Rules

- One class per file
- Match filename to class name
- Use appropriate subdirectories always
- Avoid deep nesting beyond 3
- Group related files logically

## Asset Organization

- Place images in assets/images/
- Group by type and purpose
- Use descriptive folder names
- Reference from pubspec.yaml correctly
- Maintain consistent structure

```
assets/
└── images/
    └── logos/              # As defined in pubspec.yaml
```